    {
      "source": "National Diet Library — Initial Steps toward a Constitutional State: Outline",
      "url": "https://www.ndl.go.jp/modern/e/cha1/index.html",
      "body_bytes": 15872,
      "body_sha256": "d840bc9d79d032ce99e7c4229e6a1d85b2c2cb84148a97b37453c7949bfea40b",
      "headers_bytes": 1619,
      "headers_sha256": "b304239f60e4ac29a5775faf238a8a572db36b0f5fd7da378dc248553a5c99c0",
      "normalization": "UTF-8 HTML parse, entity decoding, whitespace collapse; offsets refer to normalized text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "offset": [5013, 5229],
          "literal": "In 1868 (Keio 4), the Charter Oath (Imperial Oath of Five Articles) was promulgated; its opening words stated that deliberative assemblies would be established and affairs of state would be decided by public opinion."
        },
        {
          "offset": [4801, 5012],
          "literal": "The Taisei Hokan (formal restoration of political authority to the Emperor) of 1867 (Keio 3) was carried out in the name of founding a system of government based on public opinion centered on the Imperial Court."
        },
        {
          "offset": [5230, 5483],
          "literal": "According to the Seitai-sho (Constitution of 1868 or the June Constitution), the political organization of the new Meiji Government was to adopt the Dajokan (Council of State) system, with a view of the establishment of a parliamentary style structures."
        },
        {
          "offset": [5554, 5682],
          "literal": "Though undergoing several administrative reforms, it persisted until the Cabinet system was established in 1885 (Meiji 18)."
        },
        {
          "offset": [7955, 8111],
          "literal": "The task of compiling a national constitution by the new Meiji Government was inevitably interrupted on account of complications in the political situation."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Japan Center for Asian Historical Records — The Russo-Japanese War",
      "url": "https://www.jacar.go.jp/english/exhibition/nichiro/hikkiroku.htm",
      "body_bytes": 5379,
