      "card": {
        "id": "history-japan-easy-01a-04",
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "prompt": "Какая религиозная традиция возникла в самой Японии и связана с почитанием ками?",
        "answers": [
          {
            "text": "Даосизм",
            "note": "Институт описывает даосскую практику как путь к гармонии тела, ума и духа."
          },
          {
            "text": "Буддизм",
            "note": "BuddhaNet связывает буддизм с опытом Сиддхаты Готамы, известного как Будда; это отдельная традиция."
          },
          {
            "text": "Джайнизм",
            "note": "JainWorld относит ахимсу, или ненасилие, к философии джайнизма; это отдельная традиция."
          },
          {
            "text": "Синто",
            "note": "Jinja Honcho описывает синто как коренную традицию Японии, связанную с почитанием ками природы и предков."
          }
        ],
        "correctIndex": 3,
        "explanation": "Синто — коренная японская традиция. Jinja Honcho связывает её с отношениями жителей Японских островов с природой и почитанием ками, встречающихся во всех вещах и местах; ками включают духов природы и предков. У синто нет основателя, догмата или доктрины.",
        "source": {
          "title": "Jinja Honcho — What is Shinto?",
          "url": "https://www.jinjahoncho.or.jp/en/shinto/",
          "verifiedAt": "2026-10-13"
        }
      },
      "six_reasons": [
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "sha256": "ba3118ce920904f6db70afb19507be5afbfdd6d802fa1ac73f9fc9a678d795c1",
          "basis": "Jinja Honcho identifies Shinto as native to Japan; BuddhaNet identifies Siddhata Gotama as Buddha; JainWorld discusses Jain philosophy and Ahimsa; Taoist Institute describes Taoist practice."
        },
        {
          "kind": "editorial",
          "sha256": "ba3118ce920904f6db70afb19507be5afbfdd6d802fa1ac73f9fc9a678d795c1",
          "basis": "All options are religious traditions, and the question gives a direct, easy association for the correct choice."
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "sha256": "4207b3ab96e7d16a77c68a1d06a761694bb776f9f910d63e2fcd90573be11cb4",
          "basis": "Jinja Honcho connects Shinto with nature, things and places, and ancestral kami; it also states that Shinto has no founder, dogma, or doctrine."
        },
        {
          "kind": "editorial",
          "sha256": "4207b3ab96e7d16a77c68a1d06a761694bb776f9f910d63e2fcd90573be11cb4",
          "basis": "The explanation supplies the clues and avoids an unsupported claim about the tradition’s origin beyond its native Japanese character."
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "sha256": "5a64a7055c9b6ceddab674ee0d4f74ee976d763daac7d9c2bf4f39af7b7fc805",
          "basis": "Taoist Institute states that Taoist well-being depends on harmony of body, mind, and spirit."
        },
        {
          "kind": "editorial",
          "sha256": "5a64a7055c9b6ceddab674ee0d4f74ee976d763daac7d9c2bf4f39af7b7fc805",
          "basis": "The concise distractor note gives a useful identifying fact without implying a connection to Shinto."
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "sha256": "d4a26d6df1b03fdfa9eaba0ae15e7f3bec8fbe1efe14f0568da7f52393ad4dbc",
          "basis": "BuddhaNet names Siddhata Gotama as the person known as Buddha."
        },
        {
          "kind": "editorial",
          "sha256": "d4a26d6df1b03fdfa9eaba0ae15e7f3bec8fbe1efe14f0568da7f52393ad4dbc",
          "basis": "The note is short and distinguishes Buddhism as a separate tradition."
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "sha256": "d542c3e8739e97b1bae36f63464ab4792e42ab37ddca33c433bc4f3619e48da9",
          "basis": "JainWorld presents Ahimsa or non-violence in its Jain philosophy material."
        },
        {
          "kind": "editorial",
          "sha256": "d542c3e8739e97b1bae36f63464ab4792e42ab37ddca33c433bc4f3619e48da9",
          "basis": "The note differentiates Jainism without making an unsupported geographical claim."
        },
        {
          "kind": "source",
          "sha256": "47f1abcc08d20934ec55a0c3106bb76d5f64342008f86720d65bf6db3a6e3780",
          "basis": "Jinja Honcho describes Shinto as native to Japan and connects kami with nature and ancestors."
        },
        {
          "kind": "editorial",
          "sha256": "47f1abcc08d20934ec55a0c3106bb76d5f64342008f86720d65bf6db3a6e3780",
          "basis": "The correct option and explanation directly connect the answer to the question’s clues."
        }
      ],
      "classification": {
        "difficulty": "easy",
        "basis": "Recognize Shinto from its Japanese roots and kami worship."
      }
    },
